Appendix C

Lyapunov Theory for the Double Integrator

C.1 Closed‑loop system. For the double integrator \ddot y=u with state x=(y,\dot y)^\top, the linear state feedback u=-Kx with K=(k_1,k_2) yields the closed‑loop matrix

A_{\text{cl}}=\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\0&0\end{pmatrix}-\begin{pmatrix}0\\1\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}k_1&k_2\end{pmatrix}
=\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\-k_1&-k_2\end{pmatrix}.

C.2 Lyapunov equation. With Q=I_2, the equation PA_{\text{cl}}+A_{\text{cl}}^\top P=-I has a unique solution P\succ0 if and only if k_1>0,k_2>0. Writing P=\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\b&c\end{pmatrix}, the system is

\begin{aligned}
-2bk_1 &= -1,\\
a - bk_2 - ck_1 &= 0,\\
2b - 2ck_2 &= -1.
\end{aligned}

Solving gives

b=\frac1{2k_1},\qquad
c=\frac{1+k_1}{2k_1k_2},\qquad
a=\frac{k_1^2+k_1+k_2^2}{2k_1k_2}. \tag{C.1}

The determinant is

\det P = ac-b^2 = \frac{(k_1+1)^2+k_2^2}{4k_1k_2^2}. \tag{C.2}

C.3 Inverse matrix. Using \det P, we obtain

P^{-1} = \frac{1}{\det P}\begin{pmatrix} c & -b \\ -b & a \end{pmatrix}
= \frac{4k_1k_2^2}{(k_1+1)^2+k_2^2}
\begin{pmatrix}
\frac{1+k_1}{2k_1k_2} & -\frac1{2k_1} \\[4pt]
-\frac1{2k_1} & \frac{k_1^2+k_1+k_2^2}{2k_1k_2}
\end{pmatrix}. \tag{C.3}

