Appendix G

Smoothness and Immersion Conditions

G.1 Smoothness of \mathcal{K}_0. When the certificate condition is expressed as F(m,\pi,c)=0 with 0 a regular value, \mathcal{K}_0 is an embedded submanifold. For neural certificates verified by SMT/CEGIS, the set is semialgebraic; a stratified treatment (Chapter 8) is more faithful.

G.2 Immersion condition. The condition \operatorname{rank}(d\Phi_x)=\dim\mathcal{K} guarantees that \Phi locally embeds \mathcal{K} into \mathcal{C}. When \Phi fails to be an immersion at some points, those points form the certificate wall, and a new certificate type (a new stratum) may be required.

